WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.560
Zoro is a sword god who has become one&nbsp;
of the ABSOLUTE STRONGEST FIGHTERS in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.300
entire story with his top-tier swordsmanship&nbsp;
and insane will power. But you cannot deny&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.080
that he has fallen behind Luffy because&nbsp;
of his captain’s incredible devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.780
powers. So you know what? To even&nbsp;
the playing field we are going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:21.360
give Zoro a simply broken devil fruit to&nbsp;
see just how overpowered he would become.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.300
And before we see all the&nbsp;
insane changes to Zoro’s story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.400
which includes an incredible twist about a&nbsp;
certain black-haired swordswomen, we first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.940
have to ask the most IMPORTANT QUESTION:&nbsp;
Which devil fruit is perfect for Zoro?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:40.560
Which if you ask this question online, many common&nbsp;
fruits that people want to give Zoro are pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:46.320
good options. These include Mr. 1’s Dice fruit,&nbsp;
which turns the user into a literal blade human,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:54.420
or Nico Robin’s flower fruit which would allow him&nbsp;
to sprout more arms to fight with, but honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.420 --> 00:01:00.840
both of these powers don’t add that much to Zoro’s&nbsp;
current fighting style. I mean why does Zoro need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.940
to turn his arm into a blade when he already&nbsp;
has three ridiculously powerful swords to fight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:11.400
with? Likewise, sure you could say that if Zoro&nbsp;
had more arms he could wield even more swords,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.940
kinda like this octopus dude here, but then again&nbsp;
he pretty much already has this power when he uses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:24.540
his ultimate Ashura technique, which gives him&nbsp;
more arms and umm… mouths. Which is actually kinda&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:29.580
hilarious now that I saw it out loud. But anyway,&nbsp;
now that he has unlocked his advanced conqueror’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.900
haki, we’ll probably be seeing him bust out&nbsp;
this technique way more often in the future.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:40.500
So no Dice fruit, and no Flower fruit. So which&nbsp;
one is it? Personally, I think the Gravity fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:45.720
would be absolutely devastating when combined&nbsp;
with Zoro’s sword skills, but since we’ve already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:51.360
seen what this fruit can do in the hands of a&nbsp;
master swordsman, let’s skip this one as well.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:56.820
This brings us to our final candidates, which are&nbsp;
going to COMPLETELY BLOW YOUR MIND. And the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.820 --> 00:02:03.060
one is a brand new devil fruit that I completely&nbsp;
made up while researching for this video. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.142 --> 00:02:22.242
familiar, that’s because you might have heard this&nbsp;
name during discussions about the Wano arc. That’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:27.762
because he is the real-world inspiration for one&nbsp;
of the samurai Oden’s legendary swords: Ame no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:34.542
Habikiri. And even though Zoro doesn’t currently&nbsp;
own this sword, I still think it’s fitting since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.542 --> 00:02:40.782
Susanoo was a mythical swordsman god. However,&nbsp;
the MAIN POWER that is associated with Susanoo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.782 --> 00:02:47.442
is the power of storms, which means that if Zoro&nbsp;
ate this fruit, then he would unlock the ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.442 --> 00:02:53.862
to summon wind, rain, lightning, and tons of other&nbsp;
weather based powers. And if you know ANYTHING&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.862 --> 00:03:00.282
about one piece, then you should realize what a&nbsp;
truly OP power this would be in a world covered in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.282 --> 00:03:05.922
oceans, especially if he combined these elemental&nbsp;
abilities into his sword fighting techniques.

00:03:05.922 --> 00:03:10.902
But then I got to thinking that this fruit&nbsp;
wouldn’t change the one piece story a ton because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.902 --> 00:03:17.082
it doesn’t exist in One Piece, which is how&nbsp;
I ultimately decided that THE PERFECT devil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.082 --> 00:03:27.282
fruit for Zoro is the legendary Darkness Logia&nbsp;
fruit. And OH MY GOD, this is going to change&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.282 --> 00:03:32.622
EVERYTHING. First of all, this power gives Zoro&nbsp;
the ability to send out waves of darkness that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.622 --> 00:03:39.282
can suck in anything including buildings,&nbsp;
land, people, and much more to be crushed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.282 --> 00:03:46.722
in his darkness and then spit back out. But&nbsp;
that’s not the most important power for Zoro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.722 --> 00:03:52.062
because the number one most incredible ability&nbsp;
this would give him is to suck in devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.062 --> 00:03:58.962
users and basically turn off their powers while he&nbsp;
is touching them. Which is an INSANE ability for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.962 --> 00:04:04.182
our green haired swordsman. And even though this&nbsp;
fruit makes him absorb all the damage he receives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.182 --> 00:04:10.722
Zoro is such a high-durability tank anyway&nbsp;
that this downside isn’t really a problem.

00:04:11.442 --> 00:04:15.522
Now we get to the most mind-blowing part&nbsp;
of giving Zoro the Darkness devil fruit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.522 --> 00:04:22.362
which is all of the TRULY WILD changes it will&nbsp;
have on the story. And I personally thought it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:26.022
would be pretty boring just to give him a&nbsp;
power boost and follow the normal storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.022 --> 00:04:30.642
because honestly that would mean everything&nbsp;
is just way too easy for the straw hats. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.642 --> 00:04:36.822
instead I dug deep and figured out some actual&nbsp;
changes that just make way too much sense,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.822 --> 00:04:43.182
which includes a twist I’ve never&nbsp;
heard in any one piece discussion EVER.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:48.882
And we’ll start with Zoro as a child, where&nbsp;
much like Luffy he has somehow accidentally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.882 --> 00:04:55.002
eaten his devil fruit. Which means that&nbsp;
he’ll be practicing swordsmanship in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.002 --> 00:05:00.582
dojo in the East Blue while also learning how&nbsp;
to control his wildly destructive devil fruit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.582 --> 00:05:06.102
powers. Hopefully they have good insurance.&nbsp;
But now for the most shocking twist of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.102 --> 00:05:11.922
let’s imagine that during this period Darkness&nbsp;
Zoro somehow defeats the most powerful enemy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.922 --> 00:05:19.242
in the story… the stairs. And by defeating this&nbsp;
legendary monster, Zoro’s childhood friend Kuina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.782 --> 00:05:26.322
gets to live. All jokes aside, Kuina being&nbsp;
alive and *cough* not as Tashigi is going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.322 --> 00:05:31.362
have massive implications for the rest of the&nbsp;
story. So now let’s skip ahead several years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.362 --> 00:05:35.742
where Zoro and his equally powerful&nbsp;
friend are ready to set out to sea.

00:05:35.742 --> 00:05:40.482
At this point, I think Zoro would have gotten&nbsp;
much better at swordsmanship and mastered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.482 --> 00:05:45.582
basics of his devil fruit, while Kuina is just&nbsp;
a super powerful swordswoman. And of course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.582 --> 00:05:50.622
they still duel each other constantly, but at&nbsp;
this point I have to believe Zoro would have at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.622 --> 00:05:55.482
least defeated her a few times. Although I have to&nbsp;
point out that he probably doesn’t allow himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.482 --> 00:06:00.822
to use his devil fruit whenever he fights a pure&nbsp;
swordsman. You know, the whole bushido thing.

00:06:00.822 --> 00:06:05.862
So they both set off for adventure, but&nbsp;
tragedy is going to strike IMMEDIATELY.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.862 --> 00:06:09.822
That’s because we all know Zoro can’t&nbsp;
follow directions to save his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.822 --> 00:06:13.302
so when they split up to take down&nbsp;
some pirates on a random island,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.962 --> 00:06:20.802
Darkness Zoro somehow ends up on a completely&nbsp;
different island and is lost from his childhood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.802 --> 00:06:27.522
friend. This unfortunately means that they aren’t&nbsp;
going to reunite for quite some time, but just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.522 --> 00:06:33.102
wait for the unbelievable turn of events when&nbsp;
they do find each other in just a few minutes.

00:06:33.702 --> 00:06:40.902
At this point, Zoro will still be a bounty hunter.&nbsp;
And because of his awesome darkness powers, he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.902 --> 00:06:47.022
easily suck groups of pirates into his darkness&nbsp;
pocket dimension and then spit them back out to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.022 --> 00:06:52.962
collect the bounties at a marine base. And this&nbsp;
combination of his incredible sword skills and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.962 --> 00:06:58.662
his devil fruit abilities absolutely skyrockets&nbsp;
his reputation SO MUCH that the world government&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.202 --> 00:07:05.142
offers him a position as a Warlord. Which he&nbsp;
normally wouldn’t accept because he wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.142 --> 00:07:09.762
want to be ordered around by the marines, but&nbsp;
on the other hand he might think that accepting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:15.822
the position would earn him a shot at dueling&nbsp;
the world’s strongest swordsman, Mihawk. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.822 --> 00:07:23.982
let’s assume that Zoro becomes a Warlord and gets&nbsp;
his wish to square off against Mihawk. But man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.982 --> 00:07:31.962
this was a very bad idea, because Darkness Zoro&nbsp;
would get absolutely destroyed, just like in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.962 --> 00:07:38.142
the original story. Even if he used his devil&nbsp;
fruit, which I don’t think he would, Mihawk is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.142 --> 00:07:44.862
just in a different galaxy in terms of skills at&nbsp;
this point, so Zoro would be helplessly crushed.

00:07:44.862 --> 00:07:49.902
Which would leave him absolutely furious,&nbsp;
but he would probably now have even more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.902 --> 00:07:56.022
motivation to grow stronger. But after&nbsp;
some time to heal up, he ghosts the World&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.022 --> 00:08:00.702
Government since he already got his shot&nbsp;
at Mihawk. Then the government would most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.702 --> 00:08:09.342
likely strip away his Warlord status and label&nbsp;
him a pirate. Hmm, well that didn’t last long.

00:08:10.062 --> 00:08:16.122
Now at this point he would probably head into the&nbsp;
Grand Line so he can fight against strong pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.122 --> 00:08:20.982
but come on this is Zoro we are talking&nbsp;
about, so THE ONLY WAY he EVER makes it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.982 --> 00:08:28.542
to the Grand Line is if he finds a talented&nbsp;
navigator. So let’s say he randomly picks up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.542 --> 00:08:34.182
Navigator Manny over here, who doesn’t really&nbsp;
care about fighting but sure loves to drink,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.182 --> 00:08:39.222
and heads up Reverse Mountain into the Grand&nbsp;
Line. Which if you haven’t realized by now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.222 --> 00:08:45.042
this means that Zoro completely missed&nbsp;
out on joining the Straw Hat crew. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.042 --> 00:08:48.582
don’t worry because he is going&nbsp;
to meet up with them VERY SOON.

00:08:48.582 --> 00:08:51.822
Damn, this story is about to get weird.

00:08:51.822 --> 00:08:57.222
Now that Darkness Zoro is in the Grand Line with&nbsp;
his Navigator Manny, he is going to ABSOLUTELY&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.222 --> 00:09:03.282
CRUSH some strong opponents to take out his&nbsp;
frustration at losing to Mihawk. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.282 --> 00:09:08.022
remember that even though the World Government&nbsp;
has labeled him a pirate, his only true goal is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.022 --> 00:09:13.107
to become the world’s strongest swordsman. So I&nbsp;
can imagine him seeking out any strong pirate who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.107 --> 00:09:18.702
is also a swordsman such as Trafalgar Law or Basil&nbsp;
Hawkins who are members of the Worst Generation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.702 --> 00:09:25.302
and even strong marines such as Captain T-Bone.&nbsp;
And while&nbsp; Darkness Zoro should win these battles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:25.302 --> 00:09:29.142
he wouldn’t care about turning in the&nbsp;
pirates for bounties since he has already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.142 --> 00:09:33.942
been labeled a pirate at this point so he&nbsp;
couldn’t make any money off the bounties.

00:09:33.942 --> 00:09:39.402
But all this means that Darkness Zoro’s&nbsp;
name is spreading around Paradise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.362 --> 00:09:45.582
and it is inevitable that he will eventually&nbsp;
meet up with the Straw Hat Crew. Perhaps he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.582 --> 00:09:51.762
sails over to Alabasta to fight Mr. 1 only to&nbsp;
find that the blade man has already been defeated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.762 --> 00:09:57.762
by the Straw Hat Crew, and in particular,&nbsp;
the Straw Hat’s newest swordswomen, Kuina.

00:09:57.762 --> 00:10:03.462
Yup, that’s right. Zoro’s spot on the crew was&nbsp;
taken by none other than his childhood friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.462 --> 00:10:09.042
who was recruited by Luffy sometime during the&nbsp;
East Blue Saga. So while Zoro is pissed about not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.042 --> 00:10:15.882
being able to fight Mr. 1, he is SUPER EXCITED&nbsp;
to see his long lost friend. So of course he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.882 --> 00:10:20.742
greets her by challenging her to a duel, and who&nbsp;
knows at this point who would come out on top,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.742 --> 00:10:26.502
but whatever the outcome in the end Zoro would&nbsp;
probably end up partying with the Straw Hat crew.

00:10:26.502 --> 00:10:31.122
But these reunited friends are not going to&nbsp;
be able to enjoy their happy meeting for long.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.122 --> 00:10:35.682
Because while Zoro has been going around making a&nbsp;
name for himself, you might have wondered what’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.682 --> 00:10:40.842
going on with the original owner of the Darkness&nbsp;
fruit. Oh boy, get ready for this one. Because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.842 --> 00:10:46.662
remember that Blackbeard spent literal decades&nbsp;
searching for this fruit while on the Emperor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.662 --> 00:10:52.722
Whitebeard’s crew. So once he hears that the&nbsp;
Darkness fruit is being used by Zoro, he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.722 --> 00:10:56.982
instantly going to come after the green haired&nbsp;
swordsman. And while Blackbeard might actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.982 --> 00:11:02.742
surprise you with his strength - remember he did&nbsp;
give young shanks his scars - I’m not too sure if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.742 --> 00:11:09.222
Blackbeard would win a straight up fight. Which&nbsp;
means he’ll do what he always does. Set a trap.

00:11:09.222 --> 00:11:14.022
And there are many ways that this could go,&nbsp;
but here’s a scenario that I think makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.022 --> 00:11:17.922
a lot of sense. As Zoro and Manny sail&nbsp;
around getting closer to the New World,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.922 --> 00:11:24.222
they suddenly get a very strange call on their&nbsp;
transponder snail that instantly sends Zoro into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.222 --> 00:11:30.042
a rampage. It turns out that Blackbeard has&nbsp;
kidnapped Zoro’s childhood sensei, Koushirou,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.042 --> 00:11:36.642
and is holding him hostage on a nearby island. So&nbsp;
Zoro and Manny instantly sail to the island and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.642 --> 00:11:43.122
find Koushirou trapped in a cage. Of course, Zoro&nbsp;
slices through the bars, but as he does Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.122 --> 00:11:49.722
pops up behind him and traps Zoro in seastone&nbsp;
handcuffs. Now Manny tries to defend his captain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.722 --> 00:11:55.662
but he’s not much of a fighter, which means that&nbsp;
Blackbeard has a free shot at the weakened Zoro.

00:11:55.662 --> 00:12:01.062
This is not looking good at all until suddenly&nbsp;
Blackbeard’s pistol gets chopped in half as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.062 --> 00:12:09.402
Kuina turns up to save her longtime rival and&nbsp;
father. And as she frees Zoro from the handcuffs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.402 --> 00:12:12.762
she reveals that she had heard about her&nbsp;
missing father and was tracking him down&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.762 --> 00:12:17.382
all this time. Then together they&nbsp;
destroy Blackbeard and then depart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.382 --> 00:12:21.702
the island. This means Koushirou can go&nbsp;
home, Kuina goes back to the Straw Hats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:21.702 --> 00:12:26.142
and an embarrassed Zoro heads out to find&nbsp;
some pirates to take out his frustration.

00:12:26.682 --> 00:12:32.202
So this turn of events means no more Blackbeard is&nbsp;
going to MASSIVELY change the rest of the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.202 --> 00:12:38.262
and also means that you should subscribe to the&nbsp;
channel for more one piece content like this.

00:12:38.262 --> 00:12:44.562
Now let’s jump ahead a few years because at this&nbsp;
point there was no Marineford and no timeskip,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.562 --> 00:12:52.062
so Zoro is going to continue to seek out strong&nbsp;
opponents to get stronger. But there is one major&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.062 --> 00:12:57.042
question that we simply must answer. Because&nbsp;
remember that during the timeskip Zoro laid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.042 --> 00:13:03.402
down his pride to ask Mihawk to train him. BUT he&nbsp;
only did this because of his loyalty to Luffy and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.402 --> 00:13:11.622
the crew. So, would Darkness Zoro still seek out&nbsp;
a swordmaster to train him if he is on his own?

00:13:11.622 --> 00:13:17.322
Honestly, I think the answer is no. That means&nbsp;
that he would have to learn haki on his own, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.322 --> 00:13:22.902
I think is fairly reasonable for him to do as long&nbsp;
as he is clashing with strong fighters in the New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:22.902 --> 00:13:27.822
World. And speaking of strong fighters, he might&nbsp;
run into the Straw Hats and clash with Kuina a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.822 --> 00:13:32.682
more times, or I could even see him challenging&nbsp;
other members of the Supernova such as Euastas Kid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.682 --> 00:13:37.482
and his spinning-blade Vice Captain, Killer,&nbsp;
who he fought in the original story anyway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.482 --> 00:13:43.002
Although Kid would be a tough matchup for Zoro&nbsp;
because of his magnetism devil fruit, so Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.002 --> 00:13:51.762
might have to rely on his darkness powers to win&nbsp;
this matchup. Another very reasonable opponent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.762 --> 00:13:56.622
for him to have frequent clashes with would be&nbsp;
someone like Vista from the Whitebeard pirates,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.622 --> 00:14:02.142
who was a strong enough swordsman to clash with&nbsp;
Mihawk during the original war at Marineford.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.142 --> 00:14:07.182
But since we’re talking about Whitebeard, we&nbsp;
have to mention that this Yonko crew is only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.182 --> 00:14:13.662
still together because Marineford never occurred.&nbsp;
Which means that Whitebeard is alive, for now.

00:14:13.662 --> 00:14:19.722
However, at this point Whitebeard was already&nbsp;
sick and dying, so let’s assume that he does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:19.722 --> 00:14:25.182
die from natural causes. This could lead&nbsp;
to the Whitebeard pirates disbanding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:25.182 --> 00:14:28.902
or the much more likely scenario is&nbsp;
that someone like Marco the Phoenix&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.902 --> 00:14:36.642
or Luffy’s childhood friend Ace takes over as&nbsp;
captain. Let’s just say that it is Ace for now.

00:14:36.642 --> 00:14:42.342
Now let’s assume that by this point Zoro has&nbsp;
learned haki and possibly even awakened his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:42.342 --> 00:14:48.342
conqueror’s haki, so now he is a MAJOR POWERHOUSE&nbsp;
of a fighter. This would definitely allow him to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.342 --> 00:14:52.842
defeat Vista, and if he were to take him down,&nbsp;
then it is certainly possible that the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.842 --> 00:14:58.062
captain Ace would challenge Zoro to a duel. And&nbsp;
now there are a lot of ways that this could go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.062 --> 00:15:04.662
however since Ace is a devil fruit user, Zoro is&nbsp;
more than willing to use his devil fruit in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.662 --> 00:15:11.082
clash. And honestly, Zoro has a great chance of&nbsp;
taking down Ace even easier than Blackbeard did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:11.082 --> 00:15:15.942
in the original story. Because when Blackbeard&nbsp;
sucked in Ace and took away his powers, he could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.942 --> 00:15:21.942
only punch the fire fruit user, which didn’t do&nbsp;
all that much damage. But Zoro would take this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.942 --> 00:15:27.702
opportunity to land a major slash on Ace, which&nbsp;
could mean this fight might be over very quickly.

00:15:27.702 --> 00:15:35.982
But wow, Darkness Zoro has come a LONG WAY on&nbsp;
his own! I mean we always kinda knew that he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.982 --> 00:15:41.742
strong enough to be his own captain, but with this&nbsp;
latest accomplishment he is now considered on par&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.742 --> 00:15:47.982
with Yonko tier characters, even though he doesn’t&nbsp;
have an actual crew of his own, and honestly we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:47.982 --> 00:15:53.142
can’t say that he is Yonko level yet anyway,&nbsp;
since Ace was never as strong as Whitebeard.

00:15:53.142 --> 00:15:58.182
However, now Zoro has a major problem.&nbsp;
You see, at his current level of strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:58.182 --> 00:16:02.982
there are very few characters that Zoro can&nbsp;
now truly test himself against. Basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.982 --> 00:16:08.862
only the Marine admirals, the Yonko and&nbsp;
their top commanders, and his longtime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.862 --> 00:16:14.142
target Mihawk. The problem is that he cannot&nbsp;
find Mihawk and none of the other characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.142 --> 00:16:20.982
will just let him walk right in and challenge&nbsp;
them to a fair fight. So he’s kinda stuck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.982 --> 00:16:26.982
which leads him to make the TERRIBLE&nbsp;
DECISION to try to fight Kaido in Wano.

00:16:26.982 --> 00:16:32.802
Now, we all know it is ridiculously hard&nbsp;
to get into Wano, but let’s imagine that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.802 --> 00:16:37.362
Navigator Manny has been upgrading his&nbsp;
own skills throughout all this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.362 --> 00:16:42.402
so the pair manage to make it up the waterfalls&nbsp;
into Wano. Zoro of course would want to head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:42.402 --> 00:16:45.762
straight to challenge Kaido to a&nbsp;
drinking contest… Oh, wait, no.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:46.422 --> 00:16:52.422
A duel, but at this point, Darkness Zoro probably&nbsp;
wouldn’t be able to defeat the king of the beasts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.422 --> 00:16:58.302
Even though Zoro can negate devil fruits, Kaido&nbsp;
is still massively powerful, plus he has his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.302 --> 00:17:03.462
whole crew to back him up, so unfortunately,&nbsp;
Zoro is defeated and thrown into prison.

00:17:03.462 --> 00:17:09.282
But despite what you might think, this is actually&nbsp;
THE BEST THING that could have happened to Zoro.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.282 --> 00:17:15.882
You see, in this prison is this wrinkly old man,&nbsp;
who was the yakuza boss of Wano before Kaido took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.882 --> 00:17:24.102
over. And when he meets Zoro, they will have&nbsp;
time to fix one of the major downsides of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.102 --> 00:17:29.922
original Wano arc, which was the lack of focus on&nbsp;
Zoro’s family history. Because if you didn’t know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:29.922 --> 00:17:35.202
Zoro’s grandmother was originally from Wano&nbsp;
and part of the same Shimotsuki family line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.202 --> 00:17:41.502
who were daimyos of Wano. Which means that&nbsp;
Zoro is descended from Wano’s royalty,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.502 --> 00:17:48.042
and his great uncle was even killed by Kaido&nbsp;
when the Yonko took over the country. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.042 --> 00:17:53.202
once all this is explained to Zoro, in this&nbsp;
version of the story let’s imagine that Zoro&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:53.202 --> 00:17:58.782
feels even more anger that his homeland has&nbsp;
been ruined so now he is EXTRA determined to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:58.782 --> 00:18:03.342
take down Kaido. Which is perfect timing&nbsp;
because of what is going to happen next.

00:18:03.342 --> 00:18:09.762
You see, soon after Zoro is imprisoned, Luffy is&nbsp;
also captured by Kaido. And when these two meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:09.762 --> 00:18:16.002
up in prison, there is no way they are staying&nbsp;
trapped for long. So Zoro breaks out and joins&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.002 --> 00:18:20.982
the raid on Onigashima, where he teams up with&nbsp;
Luffy, Kuina, and the rest of the straw hats to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.982 --> 00:18:25.482
take down Kaido and Big Mom. Though I’m not too&nbsp;
sure how Luffy and Zoro would team up to fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.502 --> 00:18:32.082
Would they both want to take down Kaido or would&nbsp;
Zoro be fine with battling it out with Big Mom? We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.082 --> 00:18:38.202
might never know, but one other super important&nbsp;
question we ABSOLUTELY HAVE TO ASK is if Luffy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:38.202 --> 00:18:43.782
would have even made it to Wano without Zoro. I&nbsp;
mean, this version of the straw hats have Kuina,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:43.782 --> 00:18:48.642
but Zoro’s unbreakable will kept the straw hats&nbsp;
together more than once throughout the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.642 --> 00:18:52.722
so to find out if Luffy would even make&nbsp;
it out of the East Blue without Zoro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.722 --> 00:18:56.382
I made an entire video about it&nbsp;
which you can watch right here.

00:18:56.382 --> 00:18:59.802
Shanks for watching and I’ll&nbsp;
see you in the next one.

